@startuml requirement-issue-states
' cumin works - states of a requirement issue.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: [guard] / effect, with the name of the transition in front.
' Every guard and effect names who acts. Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / a Maintainer writes the requirement

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / cumin waits for a free slot

state "planning" as Planning
Planning : do / the Planner splits the requirement

state "awaiting-plan-review" as PlanReview
PlanReview : do / a Maintainer reviews the plan and the sub-issues

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the agents work on the sub-issues

state "accepting" as Accepting
Accepting : do / the Planner checks the merged work

state "awaiting-acceptance" as Acceptance
Acceptance : do / a Maintainer decides the acceptance

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / a Maintainer answers

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready
Draft --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work\na Maintainer adds ready to a sub-issue\n/ cumin changes the label
Ready --> Planning : request the split\n[a Maintainer added ready, the blockers are closed,\ncumin has a free slot]\n/ cumin requests the split from the Planner
Planning --> PlanReview : ask for the plan review\n[no Planner runs, cumin verified the split,\na sub-issue is open]\n/ cumin notifies
Planning --> Accepting : request the acceptance check\n[no Planner runs, cumin verified the split,\nevery sub-issue is closed]\n/ cumin requests the acceptance check\nfrom the Planner
Planning --> Planning : request the split again\n[no Planner runs, cumin could not verify\nthe split, first time]\n/ cumin requests the split again
Planning --> Decision : stop the split\n[no Planner runs, and: the Planner asked\na question, or cumin could not verify the split\nthe second time]\n/ cumin notifies
PlanReview --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work\na Maintainer adds ready to a sub-issue\n/ cumin changes the label
Implementing --> Accepting : request the acceptance check\n[every sub-issue is closed, cumin wrote the\nfollow-up notes, cumin has a free slot]\n/ cumin requests the acceptance check\nfrom the Planner
Implementing --> PlanReview : ask about the remaining sub-issues\n[only sub-issues without a status label remain]\n/ cumin notifies
Accepting --> Acceptance : ask for the acceptance\n[the Planner wrote the acceptance check]\n/ cumin notifies
Accepting --> Accepting : request the acceptance check again\n[no Planner runs, the Planner wrote no\nacceptance check, first time]\n/ cumin requests the acceptance check again
Accepting --> Decision : stop the acceptance check\n[no Planner runs, and: the Planner asked\na question, or no acceptance check the second time]\n/ cumin notifies
Acceptance --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work\na Maintainer adds ready to a sub-issue\n/ cumin changes the label
Acceptance --> [*] : a Maintainer closes the issue
Decision --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready

legend right
  A box is a state: a label on GitHub, without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
  An arrow is a transition: [guard] / effect, each with its actor. The first line is the name of the transition in issue-states.md.
  Every guard reads only facts on GitHub and "no agent runs for this issue".
endlegend

@enduml
